DESCRIPTION

  Cosmopolitan Make is a fork of GNU Make that adds support for
  automatic sandboxing, resource limits, and network access
  restrictions.

ORIGIN

  GNU Make 4.4.1
  http://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/make/make-4.4.1.tar.gz

LICENSE

  GNU GPL version 3 or later
  http://gnu.org/licenses/gpl.html

LOCAL CHANGES

  - Introduce -T FILE, --time-log=FILE flag
  - Introduce $(uniq token...) native function
  - Remove code that forces slow path if not using /bin/sh
  - .SANDBOXED variable to enable pleddge / unveil sandboxing
  - .PLEDGE variable which restricts system calls
  - .UNVEIL variable which controls Landlock LSM
  - .CPU variable which tunes CPU rlimit in seconds
  - .MEMORY variable for virtual memory limit, e.g. 512m
  - .FSIZE variable which tunes max file size, e.g. 1g
  - .NPROC variable which tunes fork() / clone() limit
  - .NOFILE variable which tunes file descriptor limit
  - .ENV variable which clamps a build rule's environment to the named
    variables (plus the MAKEFLAGS family make itself needs); an empty
    .ENV clamps to the protocol set only
  - sandboxed rules automatically unveil rwc on the target's directory
    (grants derived from the graph; targets with no directory component
    still need explicit grants)
